NAME
     cgrun - run a program in a control group

SYNOPSIS
     cgrun [-n NAME] [-w WEIGHT] [-m PCT] [-M BYTES] [-P N] COMMAND [ARG...]
     cgrun -f GROUP on|off
     cgrun -l

DESCRIPTION
     cgrun puts a program in a group of its own and runs it there. A
     group has a weight (its share of the processors against its
     siblings), a ceiling (at most this much of one processor), a memory
     limit and a process limit, and it can be frozen and thawed.

OPTIONS
     -n NAME    what to call the group
     -w WEIGHT  its share, 1 to 10000 (1024 is the default)
     -m PCT     at most this percentage of one processor
     -M BYTES   the memory limit
     -P N       the process limit
     -f G on|off   freeze or thaw group G
     -l         list the groups and what they are using

SEE ALSO
     nice(1), taskset(1), vmm(1), /sys/fs/cgroup
